From b744ba19022763e9688c6b006e8cecd24e21cc18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SteveDeFacto <5148995+SteveDeFacto@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:09:49 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Linux hold: revoke queued lease permissions by epoch; free
 nothing on an unconfirmed stop

Root review (ROOT-LINUX-HOLD-REVIEW.txt) of 09ff3ed5, both concerns verified in the source flow:

1. walletSendGate checked only rec.walletHeld and the deadline. A renewal queued under an allow survived a verified
   refusal (retireForPlacement never sets walletHeld; its release queues BEHIND the renewal), and hold -> allow
   deleted walletHeld, so an older permit became valid again on the same record.
   - revokeLeasePermits: a per-record lease epoch, moved synchronously before any await by every stop (stopContainer
     first line), every (re)provision (provisionTenant), every withdrawal (withdrawService: hold, retire, held release).
   - walletSendGate binds the record object (a replacement never inherits), its epoch, its status at the decision,
     a per-deployment count of later refused/unknown wallet answers (voids a queued CLAIM, which has no record) and
     the decision deadline.
   - app-funded: the gate is asked again in the client's onSigned seam (after signing, before any relay); a throw
     there sends the lease to no relay (NotPersisted) and the renewal reports superseded.

2. walletHoldLocal freed the GPU slice and marked the record terminated even when stopContainer returned false.
   - withdrawService (before any await): status leaves running (every /x/ ingress, bridge, isolation splice and the
     egress SOCKS admit only running/claimed), established upgrade streams of the deployment are destroyed
     (new _depStreams registry in the upgrade handler) and its egress connections closed (egress.closeDeployment).
   - settleStop: the slice is freed only when stopContainer succeeded AND a fresh backend listing names no instance
     of it; otherwise it stays reserved (_stopPending, persisted; restore keeps it) and considerClaim/tryClaim
     refuse any resume, claim or replacement of the id. The reconciler confirms from its own listing
     (settlePendingStops) before reaping. A held record clears only after a confirmed stop.
   - retireForPlacement (refusal/pin) uses the same withdraw-first and confirmed-free steps; the release itself is
     unchanged (administrator refusal still enforced).

Tests: review cases in test/supervisor-wallet-unknown-hold.test.mjs (real supervisor functions, real stopContainer,
listing, stream registry and provisionTenant, real admission bundle, both senders); egress closeDeployment case with
real sockets; tenant-provision-race harness extracts the real revokeLeasePermits.
